From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] core: read the UAPI system config hierarchy
Source: Nex
Upstream: not submitted; suitable for upstream review

get_config_path only tries SYSCONFDIR "/xdg" (the administrator's /etc)
after the user files, so it never reaches the desktop overlay's
XDG_CONFIG_DIRS tiers and a package cannot ship a default under
/usr/share with a boot-time tool free to override it under /run.

Walk the same three system tiers other Nex-patched readers use after
the user prefix: /etc/xdg, then /run/xdg, then /usr/share/xdg. Keep
the existing per-prefix desktop-token then "config" filename walk,
keep the -c override untouched, and keep compiled-in defaults when
none of the tiers has a file.

diff -urN a/src/core/config.c b/src/core/config.c
--- a/src/core/config.c
+++ b/src/core/config.c
@@ -133,15 +133,17 @@
 		config_home = config_home_fallback;
 	}

-	const char *prefix[2];
+	const char *prefix[4];
 	prefix[0] = config_home;
-	prefix[1] = SYSCONFDIR "/xdg";
+	prefix[1] = "/etc/xdg";
+	prefix[2] = "/run/xdg";
+	prefix[3] = "/usr/share/xdg";

 	const char *xdg_current_desktop = getenv("XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP");
 	const char *config_fallback = "config";

 	char *config_list = NULL;
-	for (size_t i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+	for (size_t i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
 		if (xdg_current_desktop) {
 			config_list = strdup(xdg_current_desktop);
 			char *config = strtok(config_list, ":");
